{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-pro-12-1","title":"Proverbs 12:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>2:10,11; 8:17,32; 18:1; Ps 119:27,97-100; 2Th 2:10 he that. 5:12,13; 9:7,8; Ps 32:9; 92:6; Isa 1:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-2","title":"Proverbs 12:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>good. 8:35; Ps 112:5; Ec 8:8; Ac 11:24; Ro 5:7 a man. 1:31; 6:18; Ps 9:15; Isa 32:5-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-3","title":"Proverbs 12:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>shall not be established. 10:25; Job 5:3-5; 15:29; 20:5-9; 27:16-18 the root. 12; Ps 15:5; 125:1,2; 1Sa 25:33; Eph 3:17; Col 2:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-4","title":"Proverbs 12:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>virtuous. 14:1; 19:13,14; 31:10-25; 1Co 11:7,11 she. 21:9,19; 27:15,16 as. 14:30; Hab 3:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-5","title":"Proverbs 12:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>thoughts. 11:23; 24:9; Ps 119:15; 139:23; Isa 55:7; Jer 4:14 counsels. Ps 12:2,3; 36:2-4; 41:6,7; 140:1-3; Mt 2:3-8,16; 26:4; 1Co 4:5 2Co 4:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-6","title":"Proverbs 12:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>words. 1:11-19; 2Sa 17:1-4; Isa 59:7; Jer 5:26; Mic 7:1,2; Ac 23:12,15 Ac 25:3 the mouth. 14:3; Es 4:7-14; 7:4-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-7","title":"Proverbs 12:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>wicked. 11:21; 14:11; 15:25; Es 9:6-10,14; Job 5:3,4; 11:20; 18:15-20 Job 27:18-23; Ps 37:10,35-37; 73:18,19 the house. 14:1; 24:3,4; 2Sa 7:16,26; Mt 7:24-27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-8","title":"Proverbs 12:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>commended. Ge 41:39; 1Sa 16:18; 18:30; Ec 8:1; Lu 12:42-44; 16:8; 1Co 3:10-15 1Co 4:5; 2Co 10:18 he. 1:26; 3:35; 5:23; 1Sa 13:13; 25:17; Ps 132:18; Da 12:2; Mal 2:8,9 Mt 27:4,5; Ac 12:23 of a perverse heart. Heb. perverse of heart.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-9","title":"Proverbs 12:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>He that is, etc.Or, rather, as in the old translation \"He that is despised, and is his own servant, is better than he that boasteth himself and wanteth bread;\" with which the versions generally agree. That is, it is better to be in lowness and obscurity, and to support oneself by manual labour, than to want the necessaries of life, through a foolish vanity, or the pride of birth, which refuses to labour.</p>\n<p>despised. 13:7; Lu 14:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-10","title":"Proverbs 12:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>righteous. Ge 33:13,14; Nu 22:28-32; De 25:4; Joh 4:11 but. Ge 37:26-28; Jud 1:7; 1Sa 11:2; Joh 19:31,32; Jas 2:13-16 tender mercies. or, bowels. 1Jo 3:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-11","title":"Proverbs 12:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>tilleth. 13:23; 14:4,23; 27:27; 28:19; Ge 3:19; Ps 128:2; Eph 4:28 1Th 4:11,12; 2Th 3:8 he that followeth. 1:10-19; 4:14,15; 6:32; 7:7; 9:6,13,16; 13:20; Jud 9:4; Ps 26:4 Jon 2:8; Tit 1:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-12","title":"Proverbs 12:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>desireth. 1:17-19; 29:5,6; Ps 9:15; 10:9; Jer 5:26-28; Mic 7:2; Hab 1:15-17 net. or, fortress. 10:15 the root. Ps 1:3; Isa 27:6; 37:31; Jer 17:7,8; Lu 8:13-15; Joh 15:5,16 Ro 6:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-13","title":"Proverbs 12:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>wicked is snared by the transgression of his lips. Heb. snareof the wicked is in the transgression of lips. 6:2; 15:2; 18:6,7; 1Ki 2:23; Ps 5:6; 64:8; Da 6:24; Mt 27:25 but. 11:8; Ge 48:16; 2Sa 4:9; Ps 34:19; Ec 7:18; Ro 8:35-37; 2Pe 2:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-14","title":"Proverbs 12:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>satisfied. 13:2; 18:20,21; Ps 63:5 and. Isa 3:10,11; Mt 10:41,42; 16:27; 2Th 1:6,7; Heb 2:2; 11:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-15","title":"Proverbs 12:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>way. 3:7; 14:16; 16:2,25; 26:12,16; 28:11; 30:12; Lu 18:11; Ga 6:3 but. 1:5; 9:9; 19:20; Ec 4:13; Jer 38:15-28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-16","title":"Proverbs 12:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>fool's. 25:28; 29:11; 1Sa 20:30-34; 1Ki 19:1,2 presently. Heb. in that day. but. 10:12; 16:22; 17:9; 29:11; Jas 1:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-17","title":"Proverbs 12:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>that. 14:5,25; 1Sa 22:14,15 but. 6:19; 19:5,28; 21:28; 24:28; Mt 15:19; 26:59; Ac 6:13; 1Pe 3:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-18","title":"Proverbs 12:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>that. 25:18; Ps 52:2; 57:4; 59:7; 64:3; Jas 3:6-8 like. Compare. Re 1:16 but. 10:20,21; 13:17; 15:7; 16:24; Da 11:33; Re 22:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-19","title":"Proverbs 12:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>lip. Zec 1:4-6; Mt 24:35 but. 19:9; Job 20:5; Ps 52:5; Ac 5:3-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-20","title":"Proverbs 12:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Deceit. 12; 26:24-26; Jer 17:16; Mr 7:21,22; 12:14-17; Ro 1:29 but. Isa 9:6,7; Zec 6:13; Mt 5:9; Heb 12:14; 1Pe 3:8-13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-21","title":"Proverbs 12:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>no. Ro 8:28; 1Co 3:22,23; 2Co 4:17 filled. 1:31; 14:14; Jer 13:12-14; Hab 2:16; Re 18:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-22","title":"Proverbs 12:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Lying. 6:16,17; Ps 5:6; Isa 9:15; Eze 13:19,22; Re 21:8; 22:15 but. 11:1,20; 15:8; Jer 9:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-23","title":"Proverbs 12:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>A prudent. 10:19; 11:13; 13:16 but. 15:2; Ec 10:3,12-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-24","title":"Proverbs 12:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>hand. 10:4; 13:4; 17:2; 22:29; 1Ki 11:28; 12:20 but. 27; 19:15; 21:25,26; 22:13; 24:30-34; 26:13-16 slothful. or, deceitful.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-25","title":"Proverbs 12:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Heaviness. 14:10; 15:13,15,23; 17:22; 18:14; Ne 2:1,2; Ps 38:6; 42:11 Mr 14:33,34 but. 18; 15:23; 16:24; 25:11; 27:9; Isa 50:4; Zec 1:13; 2Co 2:4-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-26","title":"Proverbs 12:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>righteous. 13; 17:27; Ps 16:3; Mt 5:46-48; Lu 6:32-36; 1Pe 2:18-21 excellent. or, abundant. but. Ps 18:12,13; Jas 1:13,14; 2Pe 2:18-22; 1Jo 2:26; Re 12:9; 13:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-27","title":"Proverbs 12:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>slothful. 13:4; 23:2; 26:15 but. 15:16; 16:8; Ps 37:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-pro-12-28","title":"Proverbs 12:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PRO","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>8:35; 9:11; 10:16; 11:19; Eze 18:9,20-24; Ro 5:21; 6:22,23 Tit 2:11,12; 1Jo 2:29; 3:7; 3Jo 1:11</p>"}]}